---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import HeroCover from '../../components/HeroCover.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../../data/og'

const headline = 'How Desk started: a task folder for Slugger'
const title = `${headline} | Ouro`
const description = 'How a task folder for my OpenClaw agent grew into Desk, Crew and the three desks I work from today.'

const colorMap: Record<string, string> = {
  canopy: 'var(--color-canopy)',
  scale: 'var(--color-scale)',
  fang: 'var(--color-fang)',
  glow: 'var(--color-glow)',
}

// Every date and claim here comes from the commit history, checked October 28, 2026:
// personal desk ouro-public-web/origin-story-archeology/ (openclaw-era.md, stack-after-openclaw.md).
const entries = [
  {
    date: 'January 2026',
    label: 'A folder called tasks',
    color: 'canopy',
    content: `<p>Slugger moved into OpenClaw on January 22. Five days later his workspace had a <code>tasks/</code> folder with a backlog, an active list and a completed list, plus templates for planning and coding. Its README was titled "How Slugger manages work".</p>
<p>Coding tasks ran on their own, with Claude Code doing the work. Planning tasks were Slugger and me together, and each one ended by producing a coding task. The first active task was a checklist of component tests for the new <a href="https://mendelow.me/#spoonjoy-story">Spoonjoy</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'Late January 2026',
    label: 'Planning docs and doing docs',
    color: 'scale',
    content: `<p>On January 29 the folder split in two: <code>tasks/planning/</code> and <code>tasks/doing/</code>. A planning doc captures what we're building and why. A doing doc breaks the how into units an agent can work through on its own. Desk still uses that pair.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'February 2026',
    label: 'Taking it to work',
    color: 'fang',
    content: `<p>On February 2, Slugger and I began adapting the workflow for my job at Microsoft, where my agents ran in Claude Code. By February 16 it was two agents. The planner writes the plan with me and turns it into a doing doc only after I sign off. The doer works through the units on its own and commits after each one. I wrote about that period in <a href="/blog/stop-being-the-glue/">Stop being the glue</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'March 2026',
    label: 'Skills that travel',
    color: 'scale',
    content: `<p>Slugger left OpenClaw for <a href="/lab/story/">Ouroboros</a>, the harness I built for him, and the habit came along: the Ouroboros repository has planning and doing docs from its second day. On March 18 the planner and doer became <code>work-planner</code> and <code>work-doer</code>, the first skills in <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/ouroboros-skills">a shared skills repository</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'April 2026',
    label: 'The first desk',
    color: 'canopy',
    content: `<p>On April 16 I gave my agents at work a Git repository of their own for task state. That repository was the first desk. Its first entries were friction notes about what got in my agents' way.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'May 2026',
    label: 'Desk, and MS Desk',
    color: 'glow',
    content: `<p>On May 18 the general parts of that work became <a href="/desk/">Desk</a>, a plugin of its own: tracks, tasks, friction notes and lessons, kept in a Git repository so the work survives sessions, machines and harnesses. Five days later the Microsoft-specific parts became MS Desk, which sits on top of Desk, and my personal desk got its own repository.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'June 2026',
    label: 'The first crew',
    color: 'scale',
    content: `<p>On June 10 my team at Microsoft got a shared workspace, the first crew. The same day, my own agents learned to follow work in the crew's desk without copying it into mine. They keep a pointer and read the crew's copy when they need it, because a synced summary goes stale.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'July 2026',
    label: 'Crew',
    color: 'fang',
    content: `<p>On July 7 the shared-workspace skills moved out of MS Desk into <a href="/desk/#crew">Crew</a>, a plugin of its own. They had lived in MS Desk only because that's where the first crew was built. In a crew, everyone reads all of it, and each person's agents write only in that person's own desk.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'September 2026',
    label: 'A home of its own',
    color: 'canopy',
    content: `<p>On September 25 Desk and Crew moved into their own repository, <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/desk">ourostack/desk</a>, with their history intact.</p>`,
  },
  {
    date: 'October 2026',
    label: 'Three desks',
    color: 'glow',
    content: `<p>On October 14 Microsoft's Customer Innovation Team, CIT, got a shared repository, and it now runs as a Crew workspace. Today I work from three desks: my personal desk, my work desk, and CIT's shared workspace. Whichever machine and harness I open, I ask "where were we?", and the agent knows.</p>`,
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogImage={ogPathFor('/lab/how-desk-started')}
  canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/lab/how-desk-started/"
  ogType="article"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="author" content="Ari Mendelow" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": headline,
      "description": description,
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Ari Mendelow", "url": "https://linkedin.com/in/arimendelow" },
      "datePublished": "2026-10-28",
      "url": "https://ouroboros.bot/lab/how-desk-started/"
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <HeroCover>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      The plan lives in a file,<br />
      <span class="text-mist">where the next agent reads it.</span>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="body">
      How a task folder for my OpenClaw agent grew into Desk, Crew and the three desks I work from today.
    </Fragment>
  </HeroCover>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 -mt-8 md:-mt-12 mb-16 reveal">
    <p class="text-sm text-shadow text-center">Ari Mendelow &middot; October 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 mb-16">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-bone leading-relaxed"><a href="/desk/" class="text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow hover:decoration-current hover:decoration-2 transition-colors">Desk</a> is where my agents keep their work. It began as a folder in Slugger's workspace, five days after he moved in.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pb-24 md:pb-36">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto relative">
      <div class="absolute left-4 md:left-8 top-0 bottom-0 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-canopy/40 via-scale/30 to-canopy/40"></div>

      {entries.map((entry, i) => (
        <div class:list={["relative pl-14 md:pl-24 split", i < entries.length - 1 ? "pb-20 md:pb-28" : "", "reveal"]}>
          <div
            class="absolute left-4 md:left-8 top-1 w-3 h-3 rounded-full border-2 -translate-x-1/2"
            style={`border-color: ${colorMap[entry.color]}; background: var(--color-void);`}
          ></div>

          <div class="split-head">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-fang uppercase tracking-[0.22em] block mb-4">{entry.date}</span>
            <h2 class="font-display text-bone leading-[1.05] text-[2.25rem] md:text-[2.75rem] mb-6">{entry.label}</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="split-body">
            <div class="story-content prose-ouro" set:html={entry.content} />
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-20 md:py-32 border-t border-canopy/30 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto split">
      <h2 class="heading-section mb-10 split-head">The habit held</h2>
      <div class="split-body">
        <div class="prose-ouro story-content">
          <p>Every step kept the habit from January: the plan lives in a file, and the next session reads it. Across the public and internal product and tooling repositories, my agents and I have made about 11,000 commits and 3,700 merged pull requests since February 22.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto border-t border-canopy/30 pt-10">
      <ul class="grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-x-12 text-lg">
        <li><a href="/approach/" class="text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow hover:decoration-current hover:decoration-2 transition-colors">How I work</a></li>
        <li><a href="/desk/" class="text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow hover:decoration-current hover:decoration-2 transition-colors">Set up Desk</a></li>
        <li><a href="/lab/story/" class="text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow hover:decoration-current hover:decoration-2 transition-colors">How Ouroboros started</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .story-content :global(p) {
    color: var(--color-mist);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .story-content :global(p.note) {
    color: var(--color-shadow);
    font-style: italic;
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-scale) 30%, transparent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .story-content :global(strong) {
    color: var(--color-bone);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .story-content :global(a) {
    color: var(--color-scale);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .story-content :global(a:hover) {
    color: var(--color-glow);
  }
  .story-content :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    background: var(--color-undergrowth);
    color: var(--color-glow);
    padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  @keyframes spin {
    to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
  }
  @keyframes drift-out {
    0%, 100% { transform: translate(0, 0); opacity: 0.15; }
    50% { transform: translate(-3px, -4px); opacity: 0.05; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .ouroboros-spin { animation: spin 60s linear infinite; }
  }

  /* Removed: previously molt-left was opacity 0.4 to fade the OpenClaw
     side as a "what was shed" visual. The user found it too dim — the
     narrative is conveyed by the labels and arrow now. Both sides full. */
</style>
